1	//! Collie's page API (ADR 0085, decided in #472).
2	//!
3	//! Playwright's page API (ADR 0019) under its names, in snake case, where the meaning is the
4	//! same, with the guard's guarantees:
5	//!
6	//! - Pages, Sessions and frames are values. A [`Session`] is Playwright's context: pages open with
7	//!   `session.new_page()` or arrive as popups, and frames are reached through [`FrameLocator`]s.
8	//!   There is no active page, no frame pointer and no element handle: a [`Locator`] is resolved
9	//!   again at each use.
10	//! - Every action, and every read of one element, waits through the guard until exactly one
11	//!   element matches and is actionable, or its deadline passes; a match still ambiguous then fails
12	//!   with `target_not_unique`, listing every match.
13	//! - The engine runs a page's gestures (actions, keyboard, mouse and touch input, navigations) one
14	//!   at a time in arrival order; reads, waits, `evaluate` and answers to routes and dialogs run
15	//!   concurrently.
16	//! - A page function is JavaScript source run in the page, with one explicit argument; values
17	//!   cross as JSON.
18	//! - Routes and dialogs arrive as [`EventStream`]s the program drives (ADR 0081). Later routes get
19	//!   a request first; the first answer wins; an item dropped unanswered falls through, and past the
20	//!   last one a request goes to the network and a dialog gets Playwright's default, so a handler
21	//!   that answers nothing never stalls the page. A gesture that waits on the program (a locator
22	//!   handler's turn before an attempt, or a route's answer to a request it waits on, after its
23	//!   input) gives up its page's turn, only between its own inputs, so a handler's own gestures run
24	//!   and no two gestures' inputs interleave. An open dialog blocks input, so a dialog's answer
25	//!   comes before any gesture on the page.
26	//!
27	//! Every call is a builder implementing `IntoFuture`, with `.timeout(d)` and `.no_timeout()`
28	//! (ADR 0080); a question that never waits ([`Query`]) has neither.
29	
